1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,221
You never need a PIN to receive a refund.

2
00:00:03,221 --> 00:00:06,442
Still, people enter their PIN every day.

3
00:00:06,442 --> 00:00:10,469
And within moments, the account is empty.

4
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:14,496
Today, the story of one such evening, step by step.

5
00:00:14,496 --> 00:00:17,717
So that the next time this call comes to your home,

6
00:00:17,717 --> 00:00:19,730
you will recognize it.

7
00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:21,285
It is evening.

8
00:00:21,285 --> 00:00:24,394
Mummy had returned a mixer grinder she bought online.

9
00:00:24,394 --> 00:00:28,669
The refund has not come yet. She searches on her phone for

10
00:00:28,669 --> 00:00:32,945
the company's customer care number. One number shows up at the very top.

11
00:00:32,945 --> 00:00:37,220
Without thinking, Mummy immediately calls that number.

12
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:41,040
A very polite man speaks from the other end. Ma'am,

13
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,859
your refund is stuck, we will send it right now.

14
00:00:44,859 --> 00:00:47,915
His voice is hurried, but respectful too.

15
00:00:47,915 --> 00:00:52,116
Mummy thinks, well, at least someone is finally listening.

16
00:00:52,116 --> 00:00:54,790
And this is where the trap begins.

17
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:58,774
He says, a request will come on your UPI app.

18
00:00:58,774 --> 00:01:01,961
Approve it, and enter your PIN.

19
00:01:01,961 --> 00:01:04,352
The refund will come straight into your account.

20
00:01:04,352 --> 00:01:06,742
Mummy feels it is a little strange.

21
00:01:06,742 --> 00:01:10,328
But the man keeps saying, ma'am please hurry,

22
00:01:10,328 --> 00:01:12,320
otherwise the refund will be cancelled.

23
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:17,153
Mummy enters the PIN. A green tick appears on the screen.

24
00:01:17,153 --> 00:01:21,985
She is happy, good, it's done. Then the phone rings,

25
00:01:21,985 --> 00:01:26,818
an SMS comes. Money has left the account, not come in.

26
00:01:26,818 --> 00:01:31,650
Mummy's face turns pale. Her hands start shaking.

27
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:35,022
The man is still on the line. He says,

28
00:01:35,022 --> 00:01:39,658
ma'am it got debited by mistake, I'll send a new request,

29
00:01:39,658 --> 00:01:43,030
the money will come back. This is the second attack.

30
00:01:43,030 --> 00:01:47,245
In panic, a person does exactly what they are told.

31
00:01:47,245 --> 00:01:51,460
Just then Beta comes into the room and asks, Mummy, what happened?

32
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:55,985
Such stories are not small. According to one survey,

33
00:01:55,985 --> 00:02:01,517
the average loss for people in online fraud was about 93,195 rupees.

34
00:02:01,517 --> 00:02:07,048
That is several months of household expenses, in just one call.

35
00:02:07,048 --> 00:02:09,562
And the saddest part,

36
00:02:09,562 --> 00:02:14,590
this money is often savings from years of hard work.

37
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:17,659
So today's questions are these. First,

38
00:02:17,659 --> 00:02:21,606
why was a PIN asked for to receive a refund? Second,

39
00:02:21,606 --> 00:02:25,990
what happens at the helpline after the money is gone? Third,

40
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:29,937
when does the bank return the money? And finally,

41
00:02:29,937 --> 00:02:34,760
In the first hour, here is what you need to do to keep the loss small.

42
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:37,057
First, understand one simple thing.

43
00:02:37,057 --> 00:02:40,502
The UPI PIN is only for sending money.

44
00:02:40,502 --> 00:02:43,565
You never need a PIN to receive money.

45
00:02:43,565 --> 00:02:47,776
When someone sends you money, you don't have to do anything.

46
00:02:47,776 --> 00:02:49,690
The money just arrives,

47
00:02:49,690 --> 00:02:52,370
the way it does when a friend sends it.

48
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:57,009
Now, what was that request? It is called a collect request.

49
00:02:57,009 --> 00:03:01,648
A collect request means the other person is asking you for money.

50
00:03:01,648 --> 00:03:05,822
The screen says pay, with the amount next to it.

51
00:03:05,822 --> 00:03:10,925
The fraudster sends it saying it's a refund. You approve it,

52
00:03:10,925 --> 00:03:15,100
enter your PIN, and your money is gone.

53
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:17,414
So why did Mummy make the mistake?

54
00:03:17,414 --> 00:03:21,272
Because in her mind she was already waiting for a refund.

55
00:03:21,272 --> 00:03:24,744
The fraudster says exactly what you want to hear.

56
00:03:24,744 --> 00:03:28,987
Mummy herself told him about the order, and he just repeated it back.

57
00:03:28,987 --> 00:03:33,230
Everything seemed real. So trust came in place of doubt.

58
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:38,115
The second way is the screen-sharing app. The fraudster says,

59
00:03:38,115 --> 00:03:42,512
ma'am, please download an app, I will help you.

60
00:03:42,512 --> 00:03:46,909
That app shows your whole screen to him.

61
00:03:46,909 --> 00:03:50,817
Whatever you type, OTP, PIN, password,

62
00:03:50,817 --> 00:03:54,237
he sees it all. Without breaking any lock,

63
00:03:54,237 --> 00:03:56,680
you handed over the key yourself.

64
00:03:56,680 --> 00:04:01,650
An OTP is that short code the bank sends by SMS,

65
00:04:01,650 --> 00:04:06,167
only for you. The bank never asks for an OTP over the phone.

66
00:04:06,167 --> 00:04:10,233
No real customer care makes you download an app.

67
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:12,944
If someone says that, understand,

68
00:04:12,944 --> 00:04:17,010
there is no customer care on the other end of the line.

69
00:04:17,010 --> 00:04:19,876
The third way is the fake customer care number.

70
00:04:19,876 --> 00:04:23,151
Fraudsters put their numbers on the internet,

71
00:04:23,151 --> 00:04:26,426
under the names of big companies. Sometimes in reviews,

72
00:04:26,426 --> 00:04:30,929
sometimes on some page. People in a hurry

73
00:04:30,929 --> 00:04:32,157
pick up the first number they see.

74
00:04:32,157 --> 00:04:36,660
Always take the real number from the company's official app or website.

75
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:41,639
One thing is common in all of these: hurry. Ma'am, do it now,

76
00:04:41,639 --> 00:04:46,618
or the refund is cancelled. Sir, your account will be closed. The hurry is there

77
00:04:46,618 --> 00:04:50,691
because if you get time to think, you will catch them.

78
00:04:50,691 --> 00:04:55,670
Wherever someone rushes you, stopping right there is the smartest thing to do.

79
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:59,474
And this is not just Mummy's story alone.

80
00:04:59,474 --> 00:05:05,655
Last year the country's cyber fraud helpline received about 3.24 crore calls.

81
00:05:05,655 --> 00:05:10,410
So almost every second, there's some call or other. Fake refund,

82
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:15,640
fake customer care, fake KYC, they all come under this.

83
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:19,466
Now the second question. Where does the money go once it's gone?

84
00:05:19,466 --> 00:05:24,728
This is where Behen comes home. She checks Mummy's phone,

85
00:05:24,728 --> 00:05:29,510
reads the SMS messages. And the first thing she says is:

86
00:05:29,510 --> 00:05:32,380
Cry later, call now.

87
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:35,250
Every minute counts right now.

88
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:38,883
First understand, the money doesn't sit in one place.

89
00:05:38,883 --> 00:05:42,111
The fraudster's money goes into mule accounts.

90
00:05:42,111 --> 00:05:45,744
A mule account means an account in someone else's name,

91
00:05:45,744 --> 00:05:47,762
which has been taken on rent.

92
00:05:47,762 --> 00:05:51,798
From there, within a few minutes the money moves on, and on,

93
00:05:51,798 --> 00:05:54,220
and gets split across many accounts.

94
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:57,719
Think of a bucket of water spilled on the ground.

95
00:05:57,719 --> 00:06:01,219
At first the water is in one place, and it's easy to gather up.

96
00:06:01,219 --> 00:06:04,718
After a while it spreads everywhere.

97
00:06:04,718 --> 00:06:08,995
Fraud money is exactly like that. The sooner you catch it,

98
00:06:08,995 --> 00:06:10,550
the more you save.

99
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:13,342
That's why Behen dials 1930 right away.

100
00:06:13,342 --> 00:06:16,600
1930 is the country's cyber fraud helpline.

101
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:21,253
You call here and register your fraud complaint.

102
00:06:21,253 --> 00:06:25,907
The complaint can also be filed online on the government cybercrime portal.

103
00:06:25,907 --> 00:06:30,560
On the call, they ask you for the full details of the transaction.

104
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:33,888
What details do they need? The transaction reference number,

105
00:06:33,888 --> 00:06:38,643
which UPI ID the money went to, when it went, how much went.

106
00:06:38,643 --> 00:06:41,496
Everything was in Mummy's phone,

107
00:06:41,496 --> 00:06:45,775
because she hadn't deleted anything. So take screenshots,

108
00:06:45,775 --> 00:06:50,530
and keep the SMS messages safe. This is your biggest proof.

109
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:54,762
Then what happens? The complaint goes into a system

110
00:06:54,762 --> 00:06:58,147
that is connected to banks and payment companies.

111
00:06:58,147 --> 00:07:01,956
An alert reaches the account the money went to.

112
00:07:01,956 --> 00:07:04,495
If the money is still lying there,

113
00:07:04,495 --> 00:07:08,727
it gets stopped. This is called a freeze,

114
00:07:08,727 --> 00:07:10,420
meaning the account is put on hold.

115
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:15,693
This system works when people come quickly.

116
00:07:15,693 --> 00:07:17,610
According to government figures,

117
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:24,321
this system has stopped more than 7,130 crore rupees from reaching fraudsters.

118
00:07:24,321 --> 00:07:29,115
Think, this money was the savings of someone's Mummy, someone's Papa,

119
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:32,470
which were saved by a call in time.

120
00:07:32,470 --> 00:07:36,464
But remember, freeze doesn't mean the money comes back immediately.

121
00:07:36,464 --> 00:07:40,058
Getting stuck money back takes a process,

122
00:07:40,058 --> 00:07:43,653
sometimes through the police, sometimes through a court order.

123
00:07:43,653 --> 00:07:46,049
Keep the complaint number safe.

124
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:50,043
And don't forget to tell your bank separately too.

125
00:07:50,043 --> 00:07:51,640
That is the next question.

126
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:55,011
Third question. When does the bank return the money?

127
00:07:55,011 --> 00:08:00,067
That same night, Sister reports the fraud on the bank's official app.

128
00:08:00,067 --> 00:08:02,596
The next day, both of them go to the bank.

129
00:08:02,596 --> 00:08:05,545
Bank Uncle is sitting behind the counter.

130
00:08:05,545 --> 00:08:08,916
Mummy says softly, it was my mistake.

131
00:08:08,916 --> 00:08:13,130
But there is a rule here that few people know.

132
00:08:13,130 --> 00:08:15,340
RBI's rules tell us

133
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:19,317
how much the customer is responsible for in an unauthorised electronic transaction.

134
00:08:19,317 --> 00:08:23,294
Unauthorised means a transaction you yourself did not want.

135
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:27,713
If the mistake is the bank's, the customer's liability is zero.

136
00:08:27,713 --> 00:08:32,132
If the mistake is somewhere else in the system, it is still zero,

137
00:08:32,132 --> 00:08:33,900
but on one condition.

138
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:35,163
The condition is this,

139
00:08:35,163 --> 00:08:41,902
you told the bank within 3 working days of getting the bank's alert.

140
00:08:41,902 --> 00:08:44,428
Working days means

141
00:08:44,428 --> 00:08:49,061
holidays are not counted. This is called zero liability,

142
00:08:49,061 --> 00:08:52,430
meaning you are not responsible for the loss.

143
00:08:52,430 --> 00:08:55,787
Now an honest point. If you yourself entered the PIN,

144
00:08:55,787 --> 00:08:59,890
or gave the OTP, the bank can say it was your mistake.

145
00:08:59,890 --> 00:09:03,246
In that case, it is hard to get the benefit of zero liability.

146
00:09:03,246 --> 00:09:07,722
The loss up to the time of reporting often has to be borne by the customer.

147
00:09:07,722 --> 00:09:09,960
That's why it is important to report quickly.

148
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:13,110
So what is the benefit of reporting? Once you report,

149
00:09:13,110 --> 00:09:18,622
every loss after that time becomes the bank's responsibility.

150
00:09:18,622 --> 00:09:22,165
That means if the fraudster takes out more money later,

151
00:09:22,165 --> 00:09:25,709
the bank will pay for it. So tell the bank first,

152
00:09:25,709 --> 00:09:26,890
then think about the rest.

153
00:09:26,890 --> 00:09:31,105
And when the mistake is not yours, there is one more rule.

154
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:35,320
Within 10 working days of the bank receiving the complaint,

155
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:38,386
the money has to be credited to your account.

156
00:09:38,386 --> 00:09:42,601
This is called shadow reversal, meaning the money shows in your account

157
00:09:42,601 --> 00:09:44,900
until the investigation is complete.

158
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:48,644
Bank Uncle gives Mummy a receipt for the complaint,

159
00:09:48,644 --> 00:09:52,805
with a reference number. This paper is very useful.

160
00:09:52,805 --> 00:09:55,717
If the bank doesn't reply on time,

161
00:09:55,717 --> 00:10:01,542
so you can go to the bank's grievance desk and then to the RBI ombudsman.

162
00:10:01,542 --> 00:10:04,870
Ombudsman means the RBI officer who hears complaints.

163
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:08,480
Now, the mistake most people make.

164
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:12,090
Shame after a fraud. Mummy's first thought was,

165
00:10:12,090 --> 00:10:14,898
don't tell anyone, what will people say.

166
00:10:14,898 --> 00:10:18,509
Many people just pass their days in this shame.

167
00:10:18,509 --> 00:10:22,520
And with every passing day, the money slips further away.

168
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:27,304
How big is the cost of delay? According to one policing study,

169
00:10:27,304 --> 00:10:33,827
72 percent of digital fraud victims did not get any of their money back.

170
00:10:33,827 --> 00:10:35,567
There are many reasons.

171
00:10:35,567 --> 00:10:39,046
But a late complaint directly means,

172
00:10:39,046 --> 00:10:42,090
the money was scattered before it could be caught.

173
00:10:42,090 --> 00:10:45,830
Even in the bank's rules, delay has a price.

174
00:10:45,830 --> 00:10:48,739
If the fault was somewhere else in the system,

175
00:10:48,739 --> 00:10:52,063
but you were a little late in reporting,

176
00:10:52,063 --> 00:10:57,049
then your liability on a savings account can go up to 10,000 rupees.

177
00:10:57,049 --> 00:11:01,620
If it's later than that, the decision depends on the bank's policy.

178
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:05,782
So what to do in the first hour? First,

179
00:11:05,782 --> 00:11:09,423
call the cyber fraud helpline immediately,

180
00:11:09,423 --> 00:11:12,545
or file a complaint on the cybercrime portal. Second,

181
00:11:12,545 --> 00:11:17,227
inform your bank through the official app or helpline,

182
00:11:17,227 --> 00:11:21,909
and get UPI blocked. Third, screenshots, SMS, UPI ID,

183
00:11:21,909 --> 00:11:23,990
keep everything safe.

184
00:11:23,990 --> 00:11:26,161
And some small rules going forward.

185
00:11:26,161 --> 00:11:28,695
Never a PIN to receive money.

186
00:11:28,695 --> 00:11:32,314
Get the customer care number only from the official app or website.

187
00:11:32,314 --> 00:11:35,933
If someone asks you to download an app, cut the call.

188
00:11:35,933 --> 00:11:39,190
And for anyone who rushes you, there's only one answer,

189
00:11:39,190 --> 00:11:41,000
I'll come to the bank myself.

190
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,603
The end of Mummy's story? The complaint was made quickly,

191
00:11:44,603 --> 00:11:48,207
the receipt is in hand, the investigation is on.

192
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:51,810
Whether the money will come back or not, we don't know yet.

193
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:55,864
But Mummy is now the biggest guard in the house.

194
00:11:55,864 --> 00:11:58,116
This is not investment advice.

195
00:11:58,116 --> 00:12:02,170
It's just straight talk about protecting your money.

196
00:12:02,170 --> 00:12:03,918
Now one question for you.

197
00:12:03,918 --> 00:12:07,849
Have you ever got a call like this about a refund?

198
00:12:07,849 --> 00:12:10,908
Just write yes or no in the comments.

199
00:12:10,908 --> 00:12:15,713
In the next video, we'll talk about those credit card charges

200
00:12:15,713 --> 00:12:20,082
that quietly show up in your bill. Until then,

201
00:12:20,082 --> 00:12:22,267
PIN is only for sending.
